# API Design Guidelines

## RESTful API Conventions

### Endpoint Structure
```
/api/auth/register          POST   - Register new user
/api/auth/login             POST   - Login user
/api/auth/me                GET    - Get current user (protected)

/api/profile                GET    - Get user profile (protected)
/api/profile                PUT    - Update profile (protected)

/api/courses                GET    - Get all courses
/api/courses/:id            GET    - Get course by ID
/api/courses                POST   - Create course (admin)
/api/courses/:id            PUT    - Update course (admin)
/api/courses/:id            DELETE - Delete course (admin)

/api/news                   GET    - Get all news (published)
/api/news/:id               GET    - Get news by ID
/api/news                   POST   - Create news (user, needs moderation)
/api/news/:id/approve       PUT    - Approve news (moderator)

/api/events                 GET    - Get all events
/api/events/:id             GET    - Get event by ID
/api/events/:id/register    POST   - Register for event (protected)

/api/map/recycling-points   GET    - Get recycling points (with filters)

/api/admin/users            GET    - Get all users (admin)
/api/admin/moderate         GET    - Get pending content (moderator)
```

### HTTP Methods
- **GET**: Retrieve data (no body)
- **POST**: Create new resource (with body)
- **PUT**: Update existing resource (with body)
- **PATCH**: Partial update (with body)
- **DELETE**: Remove resource

### HTTP Status Codes
- **200 OK**: Successful GET, PUT, PATCH, DELETE
- **201 Created**: Successful POST (resource created)
- **400 Bad Request**: Invalid input, validation errors
- **401 Unauthorized**: Missing or invalid authentication
- **403 Forbidden**: Authenticated but not authorized
- **404 Not Found**: Resource doesn't exist
- **500 Internal Server Error**: Server-side error

## Request/Response Format

### Request Headers
```
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <JWT_TOKEN>  // for protected routes
```

### Success Response Format
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    // Response data here
  },
  "message": "Operation successful"
}
```

### Error Response Format
```json
{
  "success": false,
  "error": "Error identifier",
  "message": "User-friendly error message"
}
```

### Pagination (for list endpoints)
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "items": [],
    "page": 1,
    "limit": 20,
    "totalPages": 5,
    "totalItems": 100
  }
}
```

## Query Parameters

### Filtering
```
GET /api/courses?category=ecology&level=beginner
GET /api/news?status=published&category=events
GET /api/map/recycling-points?type=plastic&city=Moscow
```

### Pagination
```
GET /api/courses?page=1&limit=20
```

### Sorting
```
GET /api/news?sort=-createdAt  // descending
GET /api/events?sort=date      // ascending
```

### Searching
```
GET /api/courses?search=переработка
```

## Authentication Flow

1. **Register**: POST /api/auth/register
   - Body: { email, password, username }
   - Response: { user, token }

2. **Login**: POST /api/auth/login
   - Body: { email, password }
   - Response: { user, token }

3. **Access Protected Route**: Include token in Authorization header
   - Header: `Authorization: Bearer <token>`

4. **Get Current User**: GET /api/auth/me
   - Header: `Authorization: Bearer <token>`
   - Response: { user, profile }

## Data Models for API

### User
```json
{
  "_id": "ObjectId",
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "username": "username",
  "role": "user|organization|admin|moderator",
  "createdAt": "2025-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"
}
```

### Profile
```json
{
  "_id": "ObjectId",
  "user": "ObjectId (ref to User)",
  "fullName": "John Doe",
  "avatar": "url or path",
  "points": 150,
  "level": 3,
  "achievements": ["ObjectId array"],
  "createdAt": "2025-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"
}
```

### Course
```json
{
  "_id": "ObjectId",
  "title": "Основы переработки отходов",
  "description": "Course description",
  "category": "recycling",
  "level": "beginner|intermediate|advanced",
  "content": "Course content",
  "points": 50,
  "published": true,
  "createdAt": "2025-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"
}
```

## Validation Rules
- Email: Valid email format, required
- Password: Min 6 characters, required
- Username: Min 3 characters, alphanumeric, unique, required
- Required fields: Check on both client and server
- Max lengths: Title (200), description (1000), content (no limit)
